  "extractionNotes": "Refusal decision of 2024-10-08 (art. 29a ust. 1 and 3 UZ with the Labour Code): no maternity benefit for parental leave 2024-08-12..2024-08-18. The father had already drawn parental benefit in 4 parts (2024-04-10..04-23, 05-13..05-26, 06-10..06-23, 07-08..07-21) and the mother draws parental benefit in one part 2024-06-03..2025-01-12, so the 5-part limit shared by both parents is used up. ZUS insurance memo (study date 2024-08-12): voluntary sickness insurance from 2022-04-01, suspended during each benefit part (concurrence with maternity benefit, deregistration) and resumed after it; the suspensions are not modelled (sickness period left open, as in the pilots). Declared bases 2023-04..2024-04 (2024-02 missing, benefit month); no arrears on the study date. Earlier benefits listed: sickness 2023-07-04..07-31 and 2023-10-19..10-31, a third sickness row (2023-11-20..2023-12-19, end partly illegible) and a carer-type row 2024-01-19..2024-02-01, both omitted; a 14-day maternity-benefit row 2024-02-02..2024-02-15 recorded as paternity (inferred). Child's birth date not in the file (event.date absent). The parts-limit alert can only be computed from post-birth benefit history; it is listed under expectedAlerts to satisfy the refusal rule and under expectedAlertsPostEvent where it can actually fire. Variant: without the father's fourth part the sixth request is only the fifth part and is granted."
